<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hanafi school</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hanafi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hanafi school is one of the four main schools of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> Islamic law, named after the eighth-century jurist Abu Hanifa. It is known for its use of reasoning and was widely followed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and the Turkic world. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> patronised Hanafi jurists as part of its promotion of Sunni orthodoxy.</p></div>
